    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d130">

                <pb facs="0417" n="401" xml:id="pg401"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Secretary’s Memoranda: Lot 53D444</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1950-10-10">October 10, 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I discussed with Mr. Lovett<anchor n="1" xml:id="d130-f1"/> work which he is
                    doing on NSC 68/1.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d130-f2"
                    /> He confirms the fear that procurement has been lagging and that energetic
                    steps must be and are being taken to activate it. He also agrees that in
                    revising the figures we should put stress on the greatest possible production of
                    these important items of combat equipment prior to the middle of ’52.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
